  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Goal**\n\nI\'m starting to dissect the user\'s request for building \"ReliefRoute.\" I\'m reviewing the implementation plan to fully grasp the scope and identify key elements for a successful build. The \"Skill Check\" confirms I\'m up to the task.\n\n\n**Assessing Key Skills**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing skills. I see that `gemini-api` is critical for the agentic features, handling intakes, and route explanations. I also think `google-maps-platform` is either relevant or useful. I need to determine if it\'s the right choice compared to Leaflet or Mapbox. I\'m going to look into the skill descriptions for each to figure that out.\n\n\n**Reviewing Metadata and Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the initial setup. I\'ve decided to prioritize updating `metadata.json` with the name \"ReliefRoute\" and a detailed description. I\'m also examining the application\'s architecture. The target environment is a full-stack Node.js application. We\'re running Express and React, all inside a single container on port 3000, which has Vite and TypeScript. This means the backend will use Express in `server.ts` for handling data storage and endpoints.\n\n\n**Defining Core Components**\n\nMy focus is now on the core components. I\'m deep diving into building the optimization engine with a VRPTW solver in TypeScript; it\'ll need to handle capacities, time windows, and optimal waypoint sequences. I\'m also planning the multi-agent pipeline. I\'ve designed an intake agent for messy reports and a prioritization agent. Then, I need to design the routing optimization agent to solve the VRP.\n\n\n**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m now outlining the UI components for \"ReliefRoute.\" I envision a live, interactive map visualizing routes with urgency-based markers and animated arrows, using Leaflet/React-Leaflet, or SVG/Canvas. I\'m also planning a multi-agent pipeline monitor to show report flow and a panel for report submission. Pre-scripted demo data is also a high priority.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 866998106
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
